 "note": [
  "Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS; NT revised 2003). Its New Testament is on disk whole (ebible mirror gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh; re-verified for this job: rom/1co/php/mrk/1pe/gal/luk/act/jhn/mat return 200, 1ki/gen 404). All twelve epigraphs are New Testament. The mirror's 1 Corinthians 6:19 and 1 Peter 1:5 sit inside bridged entries (1co 6:18-20, 1pe 1:1-10) holding another verse's text, so those two reuse the wording of shipped Amharic works (source_file names them). The one Old Testament quotation, Ahab's answer at 1 Kings 20:4, reuses the full edition's wording (absolute-surrender.am.json), so the teen and full editions quote it identically.",
  "A `mined` row was re-measured against the finished text: an exact substring of at least 20 characters of the 1962 verse (or of the cited corpus file) inside that block, or, for Mark 9:24 and Matthew 26:72, the whole of the speech the verse reports, quoted exactly. Fragments that adapt the verse (Galatians 5:22a as the full edition's chapter title «የመንፈስ ፍሬ ፍቅር ነው», the chapter 9 closing prayer from Romans 7:24-25, the two-word «መፈለግንም ማድረግንም» of Philippians 2:13) are self_rendered.",
  "The English quotes the KJV; per the Amharic teens editions the epigraph cites book and verse with no version label. The 1962 text's verse boundaries differ from the KJV's in two places the reviewer will see: Galatians 5:22 carries all nine fruits (KJV 5:22-23), so the epigraph runs past the English's «faith»; and Mark 9:24 has no «Lord». Peter's «I do not know the man» is Matthew's wording (26:72), not Luke 22:57's «Woman, I know him not», and is quoted from Matthew as the full edition does.",
  "Murray's own sentences are reused from the shipped full edition (absolute-surrender.am.json, block-aligned with the English) wherever the teen text quotes them, so a few keep Murray's plural address (እናንተ) inside the quotation while the teen prose speaks to one reader (አንተ)."
